From: retro98boy <retro98boy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: rockchip: register the missing RK3562 RGA BIU gate

RGA and JPEG clocks reference aclk_rga_jdec, but the CRU driver never registers it.
The BSP supplies this gate through its separate clock-link driver.
Register TOPCRU_GATE_CON14 bit 3 with aclk_rga_pre as its parent.
This resolves the orphan clocks and enables their parent when a consumer starts.
The VO parent domain and existing critical VO clocks cover the upstream BIU dependency.

diff --git a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3562.c b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3562.c
--- a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3562.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3562.c
@@ -922,6 +922,8 @@
 	COMPOSITE(ACLK_RGA_PRE, "aclk_rga_pre", gpll_cpll_pvtpll_dmyapll_p, 0,
 			RK3562_CLKSEL_CON(32), 6, 2, MFLAGS, 0, 4, DFLAGS,
 			RK3562_CLKGATE_CON(14), 0, GFLAGS),
+	GATE(0, "aclk_rga_jdec", "aclk_rga_pre", CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+			RK3562_CLKGATE_CON(14), 3, GFLAGS),
 	COMPOSITE_NOMUX(HCLK_RGA_PRE, "hclk_rga_pre", "aclk_rga_jdec", 0,
 			RK3562_CLKSEL_CON(32), 8, 3, DFLAGS,
 			RK3562_CLKGATE_CON(14), 1, GFLAGS),
